    {
      "id": "translation",
      "html": "<h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag</a></p>  <p>Sacred to the Concordia of the Agrigentines; the republic of the Lilybaetani (set this up); Marcus Haterius Candidus proconsul and Lucius Cornelius Marcellus quaestor pro praetore joined them in dedicating (it).</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "translation",
      "html": "<h2>Italian translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\">  </p><p>Consacrato alla Concordia degli Agrigentini, la città di Lilibeo: dedicanti Marco Aterio Candido proconsole e Lucio Cornelio Marcello questore propretore</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "commentary",
      "html": "<h2>commentary</h2>  <p>  </p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "bibliography",
      "html": "<h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> 6767 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000352\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000352</a>  </li><li> Gualtherus 1624 [1625] 115 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931</a>  </li><li> Mommsen 1883 <a href=\"http://arachne.uni-koeln.de/item/buchseite/650772\" target=\"_blank\">7192</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589</a>  </li><li> Salmeri 1984 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001608\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001608</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 1988 19 tav.1, 54, 68 n.349 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001427\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001427</a>  </li><li> Wilson 1990 180 fig.151 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 1998 137 n.28 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001816\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001816</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "handnote",
      "html": " <p>Tall, slightly curved letters, mostly with minimal serifs. P is open; R is closed with long tail; E has short horizontals of equal length, slightly upward curving; M is four equal slanting strokes. In line 5 the O and C of 'procos' are intelinked, and the following O is small and mid-line. A large diagonal upward stroke is visible above the first letter of each of the civic ethnics; and a horizontal above the Q at the end of line 6. The letters all show traces of dark paint (modern?).</p> Line 1  65-71  Line 2  68-74  Line 3  70-74  Line 4  72-75  Line 5  67-72  Line 6  67-74  Line 7  74-78  Interlineation line 1 to 2  50-52  Interlineation line 2 to 3  47-51  Interlineation line 3 to 4  50-52  Interlineation line 4 to 5  50-53  Interlineation line 5 to 6  52-55  Interlineation line 6 to 7  45-52  "
    },
